     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily looks like a possible dosing error, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n**Why I'm checking:**\n- The usual adult dose of sertraline is 50\u2013200 mg/day. Most patients start at 25\u201350 mg daily.\n- 200 mg/day is the labeled maximum. A 1000 mg dose is 5 times that, which is in the range seen in overdoses. It raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QTc prolongation and seizures.\n- One extra zero is a common error, so you may have meant **100 mg**.\n\n**How would you like to go ahead?**\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I can enter this right away if that's what you meant.\n2. **Another dose within 25\u2013200 mg/day.** Tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n3. **1000 mg was intended.** Please confirm, and tell me the clinical reason, such as a research protocol or a specialist recommendation. I'll also suggest checking with pharmacy before it's verified, since the system will probably flag it.\n\nOnce you reply, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
